<tool id="pycytominer_feature_select" name="Select features" version="@TOOL_VERSION@+galaxy@VERSION_SUFFIX@" profile="23.0">
    <description>with Pycytominer</description>
    <macros>
        <import>creators.xml</import>
        <token name="@TOOL_VERSION@">1.6.1</token>
        <token name="@VERSION_SUFFIX@">0</token>
    </macros>
    <creator>
        <expand macro="creators/rmassei"/>
    </creator>
    <requirements>
        <requirement type="package" version="1.6.1">pycytominer</requirement>
    </requirements>
    <command detect_errors="exit_code"><![CDATA[
mkdir pycytominer_output &&
    
pycytominer feature_select

--profiles '$profiles'
--output_file './pycytominer_output/output.csv'
--output_type 'csv'
--operation "${', '.join($operation)}"

&& cp './pycytominer_output/output.csv' '$output'


    ]]></command>
    <inputs>
        <param name="profiles" type="data" format="csv" label="Input cell-profiling table" help= "Table with features extracted from biological images, normally after normalization"/>
        <param name="operation"
            label="Select operations"
            help="List of operation to apply to the cell-profiling table"
            type="select"
            multiple="true">
        <option value="variance_threshold">Variance Threshold</option>
        <option value="correlation_threshold">Correlation Threshold</option>
        <option value="blocklist">Blocklist</option>
        <option value="drop_na_columns">Drop NA Columns</option>
        <option value="noise_removal">Noise Removal</option>
    </param>
    </inputs>
    <outputs>
        <data name="output" format="csv" label="Pycytominer ${tool.name} on ${on_string}"/>
    </outputs>
    <tests>
        <test>
            <param name="profiles" value="04_normalize_stand.csv" ftype="csv"/>
            <param name="operation" value="variance_threshold,blocklist"/>
            <output name="output" file="05_feature_selected.csv" ftype="csv">
                <assert_contents>
                    <has_text text="Metadata_Well"/>
                    <has_n_columns n="17" sep=","/>
                </assert_contents>
            </output>
        </test>
    </tests>
    <help><![CDATA[
    **What it does**

    **Pycytominer Feature Select** removes uninformative features. Multiple operations can be applied in one call by passing a comma-delimited list.

    - **Variance Threshold**, drop near-constant features

    - **Correlation Threshold**, drop one of each highly correlated pair

    - **Blocklist**, drop features known to be unreliable across assays

    - **Drop NA Columns**, drop columns with too many missing values

    - **Noise Removal**, remove features with low signal-to-noise ratio

    Documentation: https://pycytominer.readthedocs.io/en/stable/index.html

    ]]></help>
    <citations>
        <citation type="doi">10.1186/s13059-023-03019-3</citation>
    </citations>
</tool>